Part of the Perl CLI strand (see the strand card). The Windows binary needs a Perl process layer that works there.

What does not work on Windows today:
- Process.pm: fork, IO::Select on pipes, /dev/null, SIGTERM;
- State.pm: the lock heartbeat fork;
- the hook's detached background self-spawn.

Replace these with what works on Strawberry Perl and inside a PAR binary there, for example IPC::Run3 or Win32::Process, threads or alarm-free timeouts, File::Spec->devnull.

Constraints:
- Linux and macOS behave as they do now.
- Tests cover the portable path on Linux. Windows itself stays untested until the Windows leg of the release workflow runs.

Also on Windows: Node's readdirSync returns NTFS order. That is case-insensitive, not libuv's strcmp sort, while catalog.ts:230 relies on readdir order. Confirm that Perl's bytewise sort matches node on Windows, or record the divergence.

2026-11-14 00:11 Started (worker). Design: POSIX path of run_command/spawn_detached and the fork heartbeat stay byte-for-byte; a Windows path beside them, selected by $^O (and drivable on Linux through a 'win32' argument of injected primitives, for tests). No single portable implementation keeps POSIX's timeouts/TERM/chdir+exec stages (IPC::Open3 has no cwd, no chdir stage; select() on pipes does not exist on Windows), so two paths. Windows run_command: stdin/stdout/stderr as anonymous temp files (open '+>', undef; DELETE_ON_CLOSE on Win32) swapped in at fd level (POSIX::dup2 -> SetStdHandle) around a P_NOWAIT spawn (system { $resolved } 1, @args: STARTF_USESTDHANDLES, core only), chdir around the spawn, local %ENV, own libuv-style program search (PATH; literal-if-extension, .com, .exe; no cwd-first) and own MSVCRT argument quoting (libuv quote_cmd_arg), waitpid WNOHANG polling to the deadline, kill KILL (TerminateProcess) on timeout, reported as Node reports it there (code undef, signal 15). spawn_detached: Win32::Process::Create, no handle inheritance (the hook's stdout pipe must not leak into the background child), CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP|CREATE_NO_WINDOW. Heartbeat on Windows: no fork/threads (both clone the interpreter, DESTROY runs in the clone); the holder stamps the record from the Windows wait loop of run_command (a tick, at most once per refresh).

